  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 154 AM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nNo big changes in the short term forecast today, though we are \nseeing the smoke make it a bit farther into the Snake River Plain \nearly this morning as noted by decreased visibility of 3 to 6 miles \nfrom Boise to Twin Falls. We are expecting this smoke to continue \nits eastward movement to at least Burley, if not into Pocatello this \nmorning. This smoke is expected to impact air quality today with an \nair quality alert continuing at least through today. Highs today \nwill be a bit warmer than yesterday, making it into the low to mid \n80s for most. \n\nHigh pressure will keep us dry throughout the week with no \nprecipitation in the forecast until early next week, and even then \nit doesn't look like much. Highs will continually warm up this week, \nreaching near 100 degrees on Friday afternoon in the lower \nelevations. Wind gusts each afternoon will be around 15 to 25 mph \nwith a few pockets of gusts closer to 30 mph out across the desert.",
